name: Structural / Logical Objection
description: Report a contradiction, invalid derivation, ambiguity, or structural problem in an RFC.
title: "[Structural Objection]: "
labels: ["structural-objection"]

body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        ## Before submitting

        Use this form for a specific structural or logical objection to an RFC.

        This may include:

        - a contradiction between definitions or constraints,
        - an unsupported derivation,
        - an ambiguous classification rule,
        - an internally inconsistent result,
        - a missing structural case, or
        - language that causes the model to behave inconsistently.

        General disagreement or philosophical debate belongs in Discussions.

  - type: input
    id: rfc
    attributes:
      label: RFC
      description: Which RFC are you challenging?
      placeholder: RFC-0001
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: input
    id: section
    attributes:
      label: Section or Constraint
      description: Identify the specific section, definition, constraint, or derivation involved.
      placeholder: "Constraint 2 — No Initiated Coercion"
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: objection
    attributes:
      label: Structural or Logical Objection
      description: State the specific problem as clearly as possible.
      placeholder: Explain the contradiction, ambiguity, unsupported inference, or structural failure.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: reasoning
    attributes:
      label: Reasoning
      description: Show why the current language or derivation produces the claimed problem.
      placeholder: Walk through the logic step by step.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: consequence
    attributes:
      label: Consequence for the Model
      description: What happens if this objection is correct?
      placeholder: Explain what definition, classification, constraint, or conclusion becomes inconsistent or unreliable.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: proposed-resolution
    attributes:
      label: Proposed Resolution
      description: Optional. Suggest a clarification, correction, or alternative formulation if you have one.
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: textarea
    id: additional
    attributes:
      label: Additional Context
      description: Include related Discussions, Issues, examples, references, or other useful context.
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: checkboxes
    id: confirmation
    attributes:
      label: Submission Check
      options:
        - label: I have searched existing Issues and Discussions for this objection.
          required: true
        - label: I am identifying a specific structural or logical problem rather than general disagreement with the specification.
          required: true
